# Bu dosya GitHub'daki "Cite this repository" düğmesini besler (CFF 1.2.0).
# Henüz DOI yok; Zenodo-GitHub bağlantısı kurulduktan sonra `doi:` alanı eklenecek (docs/publishing.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Circuitiary in teaching or research material, please cite it as below. It is a parameterised teaching model, not a measurement or a brain emulation."
type: software
title: "Circuitiary"
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - given-names: "Mehmet"
    family-names: "Bozkurt"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mehmet-bozkurt/Circuitiary"
url: "https://mehmet-bozkurt.github.io/Circuitiary/"
abstract: "Circuitiary is an interactive teaching notebook for small neuron circuits, with a Turkish user interface. It lets learners build and probe an eight-cell illustrative circuit and a 30-neuron anatomical subgraph of the C. elegans connectome (Cook et al. 2019 wiring data, imported locally and not redistributed), run a parameterised continuous rate model on it, and compare the effect of changed connections, time constants and thresholds in 2D and 3D views, guided lessons, a glossary, a species atlas and a circuit builder. The anatomy comes from the cited source; all dynamics are explicit teaching assumptions. It is not a measurement, a behaviour simulation or a biological brain emulation."
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - connectome
  - c-elegans
  - neural-circuits
  - computational-neuroscience
  - education
  - simulation
  - visualization
  - turkish
